<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>About &mdash; Literary Science</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
  /* ── WORDMARK ── */
  .wm {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  /* ── HERO ── */
  .about-hero {
    min-height: 85vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 8rem 3rem 5rem;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-doc-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fadeIn 1s ease 0.1s forwards;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: revealSlow 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1) 0.15s forwards;
  }

  .about-title .line-2 {
    display: block;
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: revealSlow 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1) 0.35s forwards;
  }

  .about-rule {
    width: 80px; height: 2px;
    background: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: expandLine 1s ease 0.7s forwards;
  }

  .about-lead {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 540px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fadeIn 1.2s ease 1s forwards;
  }

  /* ── DEFINITION STRIP ── */
  .def-strip {
    padding: 5rem 3rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .def-strip::before, .def-strip::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 25px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,
      transparent 0px, transparent 3px,
      rgba(242,242,242,0.04) 3px, rgba(242,242,242,0.04) 4px);
  }
  .def-strip::before { left: 0; }
  .def-strip::after { right: 0; }
  .def-inner {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .def-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .def-text {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.2vw, 1.55rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--paper);
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  .def-text em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--paper-dark);
  }

  /* ── STRUCTURE GRID ── */
  .structure {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .struct-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 4rem 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .struct-header-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .struct-header h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .struct-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: all 0.4s;
  }

  .struct-row:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .struct-row:hover .struct-num,
  .struct-row:hover .struct-desc { color: rgba(242,242,242,0.6); }

  .struct-num {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    transition: color 0.4s;
  }

  .struct-content {}

  .struct-name {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .struct-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 560px;
    transition: color 0.4s;
  }

  /* ── MIRROR STRIP ── */
  .mirror-strip {
    padding: 4.5rem 3rem;
    background: var(--paper-light);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .mirror-inner {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .mirror-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .mirror-text {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.4rem);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  /* ── PEOPLE ── */
  .people {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .people-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .people-header-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .people-header h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .person {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .person-role {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .person-name {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .person-bio {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  /* ── COLOPHON ── */
  .colophon {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3.5rem 3rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .colophon-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  .colophon-col-title {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .colophon-col-text {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  /* ── NEXT LINK ── */
  .next-page {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    transition: padding-left 0.4s;
  }
  .next-page:hover { padding-left: 3.8rem; }
  .next-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300; font-size: 0.5rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .next-title {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .next-arrow {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    transition: transform 0.3s;
  }
  .next-page:hover .next-arrow { transform: translateX(6px); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .def-inner,
    .struct-header,
    .struct-row,
    .mirror-inner,
    .people-header,
    .person,
    .colophon { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .colophon { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero { padding: 7rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
    .def-strip { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
    .struct-header { padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .struct-row { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
    .mirror-strip { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
    .people { padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .person { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
    .colophon { padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .next-page { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a href="/" class="nav-logo">Literary Science</a>
  <ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="/epistemology/">Methodology</a></li>
    <li><a href="/toolkit/">Toolkit</a></li>
    <li><a href="/studio/">Studio</a></li>
    <li><a href="/newcomm/">NewComm</a></li>
    <li><a href="/workshops/">Workshops</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about/" class="active">About</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<!-- ── HERO ── -->
<header class="about-hero">
  <div class="about-doc-label">About &mdash; LS&ndash;000 &mdash; 2026</div>
  <h1 class="about-title">An open
    <span class="line-2">methodology.</span>
  </h1>
  <div class="about-rule"></div>
  <p class="about-lead">Literary Science is a free, open methodology for reading novels as instruments of social analysis&mdash;and for building something in the world with what you see. Created by Chidi Asoluka. Developed and maintained by <span class="wm">NEWCOMM PARTNERS</span>.</p>
</header>

<!-- ── DEFINITION STRIP ── -->
<div class="def-strip reveal">
  <div class="def-inner">
    <div class="def-label">Definition<br>LS&ndash;000</div>
    <p class="def-text">Literary Science is an open epistemology for reading novels as instruments of social analysis. The methodology, the tools, and the thinking are published here&mdash;free to study, adapt, and practice in any context.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── STRUCTURE ── -->
<div class="structure">
  <div class="struct-header reveal">
    <div class="struct-header-label">What This Site Is</div>
    <h2>Everything here is yours to use.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="struct-row reveal">
    <div class="struct-num">Layer 01<br>Methodology</div>
    <div class="struct-content">
      <div class="struct-name">The Epistemology</div>
      <p class="struct-desc">The intellectual foundations of the practice&mdash;why literature from marginalized communities functions as operational technology, and how a novel becomes a tool for understanding and intervening in designed systems. Read the full methodology. Challenge it. Build on it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="struct-row reveal">
    <div class="struct-num">Layer 02<br>Tools</div>
    <div class="struct-content">
      <div class="struct-name">The Toolkit</div>
      <p class="struct-desc">Free, downloadable resources for practitioners. One-pagers, templates, and guides designed to be downloaded Friday and used Monday. No gate, no paywall, no certification required.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="struct-row reveal">
    <div class="struct-num">Layer 03<br>Practice</div>
    <div class="struct-content">
      <div class="struct-name">Workshops</div>
      <p class="struct-desc">For schools, museums, libraries, and community organizations that want to go deeper. Literary Science runs in-person workshops&mdash;from half-day introductions to year-long partnerships&mdash;to build your team&rsquo;s capacity to practice the methodology independently.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="struct-row reveal">
    <div class="struct-num">Layer 04<br>Expression</div>
    <div class="struct-content">
      <div class="struct-name">NewComm</div>
      <p class="struct-desc">The methodology&rsquo;s most complete expression. The New Community Project operates on independent school campuses, where students lead real projects with real budgets for real communities. NewComm is what happens when Literary Science transforms what an institution is for.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── WORKING PRINCIPLE ── -->
<div class="mirror-strip reveal">
  <div class="mirror-inner">
    <div class="mirror-label">Working Principle</div>
    <p class="mirror-text">The methodology is open because the work belongs to more than one institution. Anyone can practice Literary Science. Workshops exist for those who want guidance. NewComm exists for those ready to go all the way.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── PEOPLE ── -->
<div class="people">
  <div class="people-header reveal">
    <div class="people-header-label">Creator</div>
    <h2>Who Built This</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="person reveal">
    <div class="person-role">Creator<br>&amp; Director</div>
    <div>
      <div class="person-name">Chidi Asoluka</div>
      <p class="person-bio">Chidi Asoluka created Literary Science and leads its development through <span class="wm">NEWCOMM PARTNERS</span>, the organization responsible for the methodology, this publication, and the workshop practice. His work sits at the intersection of literary analysis, community development, and institutional design.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── COLOPHON ── -->
<div class="colophon reveal">
  <div class="colophon-label">Colophon</div>
  <div>
    <div class="colophon-col-title">Typography</div>
    <p class="colophon-col-text">Libre Baskerville<br>EB Garamond<br>JetBrains Mono</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <div class="colophon-col-title">Infrastructure</div>
    <p class="colophon-col-text">Built with Eleventy<br>Hosted on Netlify<br>Open source</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <div class="colophon-col-title">Contact</div>
    <p class="colophon-col-text"><a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com" style="color: var(--ink);">hello@literaryscience.com</a><br><a href="https://www.newcommproject.org" style="color: var(--warm-gray);">newcommproject.org</a><br><a href="https://www.newcommpartners.org" style="color: var(--warm-gray);">newcommpartners.org</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

<a href="/" class="next-page">
  <div>
    <div class="next-label">Return</div>
    <div class="next-title">Literary Science &mdash; Home</div>
  </div>
  <div class="next-arrow">&rarr;</div>
</a>

<footer>
  <div class="footer-left">Literary Science</div>
  <div class="footer-right">A <a href="https://www.newcommpartners.org" style="color: var(--faded);">NewComm Partners</a> property &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Contact</a> &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; &copy; 2026</div>
</footer>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('visible'); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>
</body>
</html>
